REGRESSION FOUND BY THE A/B AND FIXED IN THE SAME CHANGE. field_type_registry is
built from analysed declarations, so its keys are bare type names -- Tester, never
caddytest.Tester -- and once the constructor bound the qualified form,
_resolve_field_chain's first lookup missed. On caddy, tester.Client.Get(proxyURL)
after tester := caddytest.NewTester(t) LOST its net_send tag at two sites, which
is a true positive. _registry_type_key recovers the bare key, but only when the
qualifier is not a definitively out-of-module package: stripping a prefix off an
external type is the collision _external_package_for_type exists to prevent
(url.Values once absorbed 13 spurious in-edges into one struct). That leaves the
pre-qualifier behaviour intact everywhere except the case where it was the bug,
and it adds four net_send tags on caddy on its own.

